It depends on the type of change you want. If you want specific pause times, I think it's better to create new trajectories for each of them. But if you want them to change randomly, the just put the function on the timeout expression. Like this:

pause<- trajectory("Pause") %>% seize("P3", 10) %>% timeout(rexp(1,15)) %>% release("P3", 10)

I'm not sure if I understood your question correctly.

On Wednesday, November 8, 2017 at 1:24:04 PM UTC+1, Shereen Ashraf wrote:
> So for the timeout to automatically change according to the corresponding pause time at 60,50,1080, you would create a function?

