2017-11-08 19:42 GMT+01:00 Shereen Ashraf <sashra...@gmail.com>:
> Also, if I have two trajectories generating batches independently, how do I
> distinguish between batches coming from trajectory 1 and trajectory 2
> respectively but still have them numbered?
>
> i.e in trajectory 1, batches of 20 every 1 hour
> in trajectory 2, batches of 25 every 2 hours
>
> When running the simulation, how do I tag batches coming from traj 1 and
> batches coming from traj 2 since they are independently generated?
>
> So it looks something like this in the output:
>
>  batch0_traj1
>  batch1_traj1
> batch2_traj1
>
> batch0_traj2
> batch1_traj2
> batch2_traj2

There's a "name" argument to the batch activity, but then you lose the
numbers, i.e., the distinction among batches under the same name.
However, note that batch identifiers are merely informational and only
appear in logs or debugging information (verbose=TRUE): they are NOT
monitored. Batches are "fictitious" entities, so only arrivals are
monitored. I suggest you to rely on them, not on batches.

>
>
>
