So batches of 20 packages that seize a shuttle and then seize a
driver. "Shuttle" is a resource with capacity=10 and "driver" is
another resource with capacity=4.

> I could consider
> them as new resources, with a capacity of 20, but still I have the problem
> to simulate that they are transported in batches. There is also a question
> with the time the empty shuttle takes to come back from the warehouse, while
> the packages continue their trajectories. Any idea?

That's interesting: it would be a delayed release. I would not only
seize the shuttle(s), but also decrement its capacity by one. Then,
right before releasing it, I would activate a generator to put an
arrival into another trajectory which would spend some time (the time
it takes for the empty shuttle to come back) and then increase the
capacity by one. Schematically:

- batch 20
- seize shuttle
- set capacity shuttle -1
- seize driver
- timeout (to warehouses)
- release driver
- activate generator into other trajectory
- release shuttle
- separate
- ...

And in the other trajectory:

- timeout (shuttle coming back)
- set capacity shuttle +1

What do you think?

